ush":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/pulls/11552","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/11552","diff_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/11552.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/11552.patch","merged_at":"2019-05-25T19:38:38Z"},"body":"**What is the purpose of this pull request? (put an \"X\" next to item)**\r\n\r\n[X] Add something to the core: fixes #11035, fixes #11725 \r\n\r\n**What changes did you make? (Give an overview)**\r\n\r\nThis PR adds support for multiple processors (eslint/rfcs#3).\r\n\r\n- The `preprocess` method of processors now can return `{ text, filename }` formed objects.\r\n- The `processor` key in config files.\r\n- The `disableFixs` option in `Linter#verify()` method to disable autofix for the processors which don't support autofix in recursive calls.\r\n- The `filterCodeBlock` option in `Linter#verify()` method to filter code blocks by `--ext` option in recursive calls.\r\n\r\nThis implementation is different a bit from what eslint/rfcs#3 described because #11546 improved the configuration calculation. The current configuration calculation doesn't need file systems, so we don't need to move the application of processors to `CLIEngine`. It avoided cloning `Linter#verifyAndFix` logic to `CLIEngine`.\r\n\r\n**Is there anything you'd like reviewers to focus on?**\r\n\r\nNothing in particular.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/11552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/11552/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2351027944,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIzNTEwMjc5NDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/2351027944","actor":{"login":"mysticatea","id":1937871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXN